{"unit_id": "sub_0001", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:01,430", "end": "00:00:04,400"}, "text": "OK, so welcome back, everyone.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0002", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:04,400", "end": "00:00:07,443"}, "text": "Today, we'll go more into circuits", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0003", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:07,443", "end": "00:00:09,360"}, "text": "as you did yesterday in the afternoon session.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0004", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:09,360", "end": "00:00:12,620"}, "text": "Just this time, it's going to be circuits with extra features.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0005", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:12,620", "end": "00:00:14,880"}, "text": "On top of them are more specialized circuits.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0006", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:14,880", "end": "00:00:17,037"}, "text": "So we'll start with synaptic plasticity", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0007", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:17,037", "end": "00:00:18,120"}, "text": "in reinforcement learning.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0008", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:18,120", "end": "00:00:20,870"}, "text": "So in other words, we will model circuits", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0009", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:20,870", "end": "00:00:25,370"}, "text": "with learning rules or synaptic plasticity rules in them that", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0010", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:25,370", "end": "00:00:28,400"}, "text": "adapt over time.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0011", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:28,400", "end": "00:00:32,119"}, "text": "Now, the synaptic plasticity in general", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0012", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:32,119", "end": "00:00:35,670"}, "text": "is the adaptations that happen within synapses.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0013", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:35,670", "end": "00:00:39,050"}, "text": "And as we saw yesterday morning, synapses", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0014", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:39,050", "end": "00:00:43,220"}, "text": "is how neurons communicate with one another.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0015", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:43,220", "end": "00:00:47,420"}, "text": "So when we say that one synapse is potentiated or becomes", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0016", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:47,420", "end": "00:00:49,730"}, "text": "strengthened, then it is more it's", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0017", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:49,730", "end": "00:00:52,940"}, "text": "easier for a presynaptic neuron to communicate spikes", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0018", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:52,940", "end": "00:00:54,740"}, "text": "to a postsynaptic one.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0019", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:54,740", "end": "00:00:58,580"}, "text": "And likewise, depression or weakening the synapse", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0020", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:00:58,580", "end": "00:01:00,220"}, "text": "is the opposite of this.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0021", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:00,220", "end": "00:01:03,910"}, "text": "And we can have different synaptic mechanisms working", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0022", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:03,910", "end": "00:01:05,800"}, "text": "on different timescales within the brain,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0023", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:05,800", "end": "00:01:08,905"}, "text": "from milliseconds to even minutes and longer.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0024", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:08,905", "end": "00:01:15,230"}, "text": "And a very classic rule about synaptic plasticity,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0025", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:15,230", "end": "00:01:18,130"}, "text": "you probably have heard of this, but put forth by Donald Hebb", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0026", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:18,130", "end": "00:01:21,710"}, "text": "in the '40s about neurons that fire together, wire together,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0027", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:21,710", "end": "00:01:25,660"}, "text": "which, in other words, means that if the spike times of two", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0028", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:25,660", "end": "00:01:28,215"}, "text": "neurons are very close to one another and these neurons are", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0029", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:28,215", "end": "00:01:29,840"}, "text": "connected, of course, with the synapse,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0030", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:29,840", "end": "00:01:32,440"}, "text": "then the synapse would get strengthened.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0031", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:32,440", "end": "00:01:34,870"}, "text": "And we will see essentially different flavors", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0032", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:34,870", "end": "00:01:41,170"}, "text": "of this Hebbian rule today in the exercises.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0033", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:41,170", "end": "00:01:46,660"}, "text": "So you have seen this the corticostriatal model", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0034", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:46,660", "end": "00:01:50,620"}, "text": "in the first day's talk, and partial view of that you", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0035", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:50,620", "end": "00:01:54,480"}, "text": "have built yesterday.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0036", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:54,480", "end": "00:01:56,230"}, "text": "And essentially, this model was originally", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0037", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:56,230", "end": "00:01:57,920"}, "text": "designed to do category learning.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0038", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:01:57,920", "end": "00:02:00,770"}, "text": "And as you might remember, the task with category learning", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0039", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:00,770", "end": "00:02:05,900"}, "text": "was originating in the macaque literature, where, essentially,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0040", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:05,900", "end": "00:02:11,630"}, "text": "the monkey had to decide whether a specific dot pattern, so", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0041", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:11,630", "end": "00:02:16,020"}, "text": "a cue like this one, belongs to category left or category right.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0042", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:16,020", "end": "00:02:20,930"}, "text": "And these are the two prototypes where that essentially", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0043", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:20,930", "end": "00:02:22,710"}, "text": "generated all the stimuli.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0044", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:22,710", "end": "00:02:25,380"}, "text": "Of course, the monkey had never seen the prototypes,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0045", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:25,380", "end": "00:02:28,580"}, "text": "but the challenge was to come up with a categorization rule that", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0046", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:28,580", "end": "00:02:31,170"}, "text": "can distinguish between these things.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0047", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:31,170", "end": "00:02:34,200"}, "text": "So every stimulus here, I should say, is an exemplar.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0048", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:34,200", "end": "00:02:36,980"}, "text": "And this is a distorted image of either one of the two", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0049", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:36,980", "end": "00:02:37,530"}, "text": "prototypes.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0050", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:37,530", "end": "00:02:42,800"}, "text": "So the animals never see exactly the prototype.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0051", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:42,800", "end": "00:02:47,270"}, "text": "So, yeah, the animal has never seen the prototype.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0052", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:47,270", "end": "00:02:50,990"}, "text": "Just by trial and error and taking actions and receiving", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0053", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:50,990", "end": "00:02:54,200"}, "text": "feedback, it has to learn how to distinguish between the two", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0054", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:54,200", "end": "00:02:54,750"}, "text": "categories.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0055", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:54,750", "end": "00:02:58,470"}, "text": "And this, we claim, is essentially", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0056", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:02:58,470", "end": "00:03:01,090"}, "text": "driven by synaptic plasticity in the animal's brain.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0057", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:01,090", "end": "00:03:05,565"}, "text": "And this is what the full corticostriatal model building", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0058", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:05,565", "end": "00:03:08,525"}, "text": "neuron blocks has in it as well.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0059", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:08,525", "end": "00:03:10,650"}, "text": "So here, I'm just showing you the model again, just", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0060", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:10,650", "end": "00:03:13,830"}, "text": "to remind you of the structure and also highlight", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0061", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:13,830", "end": "00:03:16,616"}, "text": "a few components which have to do with the task.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0062", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:16,616", "end": "00:03:19,250"}, "text": "So the stimulus coming into the model, this", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0063", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:19,250", "end": "00:03:20,250"}, "text": "is [INAUDIBLE] stimulus.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0064", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:20,250", "end": "00:03:22,420"}, "text": "You build [INAUDIBLE] stimuli yesterday.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0065", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:22,420", "end": "00:03:25,720"}, "text": "So these are the dot patterns coming in to visual cortex.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0066", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:25,720", "end": "00:03:29,280"}, "text": "And after the cortex to the striatum connections", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0067", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:29,280", "end": "00:03:31,330"}, "text": "and to other subcortical regions,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0068", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:31,330", "end": "00:03:33,900"}, "text": "we have the final action, which is the saccade", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0069", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:33,900", "end": "00:03:36,540"}, "text": "because the monkey chooses left or right by looking", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0070", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:36,540", "end": "00:03:38,430"}, "text": "at the left or right direction.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0071", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:38,430", "end": "00:03:42,220"}, "text": "And after the action, we also have the behavioral feedback,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0072", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:42,220", "end": "00:03:44,520"}, "text": "which is reward or no reward according", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0073", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:44,520", "end": "00:03:47,520"}, "text": "to the other choice made.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0074", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:47,520", "end": "00:03:51,790"}, "text": "So these are all part of the model, so within your block's", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0075", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:51,790", "end": "00:03:55,620"}, "text": "model actual behavioral tasks, and link them", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0076", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:55,620", "end": "00:03:59,260"}, "text": "to a circuit model with no problem.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0077", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:03:59,260", "end": "00:04:01,880"}, "text": "And as I mentioned yesterday as well,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0078", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:01,880", "end": "00:04:05,140"}, "text": "this model was built on principles", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0079", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:05,140", "end": "00:04:09,410"}, "text": "about structure and function that we have about the brain.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0080", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:09,410", "end": "00:04:12,550"}, "text": "And it was constrained by specific parameters", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0081", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:12,550", "end": "00:04:14,750"}, "text": "that we got from the literature.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0082", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:14,750", "end": "00:04:17,839"}, "text": "It was never directly fitted to data from this task.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0083", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:17,839", "end": "00:04:21,003"}, "text": "Yet it can match both the physiological elements", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0084", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:21,003", "end": "00:04:23,170"}, "text": "of the task, as you can see here, in the [INAUDIBLE]", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0085", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:23,170", "end": "00:04:25,160"}, "text": "LFB and its spectrogram.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0086", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:25,160", "end": "00:04:28,425"}, "text": "And also, it can match the learning behavior over time.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0087", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:30,940", "end": "00:04:36,040"}, "text": "And it can actually match both the [INAUDIBLE]", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0088", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:36,040", "end": "00:04:39,190"}, "text": "phase and the behavior because of the learning rules", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0089", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:39,190", "end": "00:04:41,810"}, "text": "that help it adapt over trials.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0090", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:41,810", "end": "00:04:45,520"}, "text": "And this model includes both LTP, Long-Term Potentiation,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0091", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:45,520", "end": "00:04:48,250"}, "text": "in the corticocortical synapses, that", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0092", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:48,250", "end": "00:04:50,920"}, "text": "is, the synapses between the visual cortex and the anterior", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0093", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:50,920", "end": "00:04:51,940"}, "text": "cortex.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0094", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:51,940", "end": "00:04:58,020"}, "text": "And it also includes corticostriatal synapses", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0095", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:04:58,020", "end": "00:05:00,430"}, "text": "that can do both LTP or LTD.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0096", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:00,430", "end": "00:05:05,760"}, "text": "And these are also modulated by dopamine between the anterior", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0097", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:05,760", "end": "00:05:08,340"}, "text": "cortex and the striatum here.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0098", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:08,340", "end": "00:05:11,200"}, "text": "And we'll get into more detail about these.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0099", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:11,200", "end": "00:05:15,850"}, "text": "And as a note in your blogs, we call this units synaptic rules,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0100", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:15,850", "end": "00:05:17,400"}, "text": "learning rules because this is all", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0101", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:17,400", "end": "00:05:20,700"}, "text": "in the context of decision-making.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0102", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:20,700", "end": "00:05:23,160"}, "text": "So the learning rule is essentially the gradient", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0103", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:23,160", "end": "00:05:28,050"}, "text": "that the synaptic weights follow to adapt over time.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0104", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:28,050", "end": "00:05:32,670"}, "text": "So first with the corticocortical LTP,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0105", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:32,670", "end": "00:05:36,840"}, "text": "this is a form of Hebbian learning, as you can see here", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0106", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:36,840", "end": "00:05:38,700"}, "text": "with this term, the LTP.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0107", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:38,700", "end": "00:05:40,500"}, "text": "The S's here are the activities of", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0108", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:40,500", "end": "00:05:42,580"}, "text": "the presynaptic and postsynaptic neuron.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0109", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:42,580", "end": "00:05:45,280"}, "text": "And it also includes an extra reversal term,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0110", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:45,280", "end": "00:05:48,390"}, "text": "which essentially means that this term is actually", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0111", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:48,390", "end": "00:05:51,270"}, "text": "dependent on dopamine released in VTA.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0112", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:51,270", "end": "00:05:54,600"}, "text": "So what's happening here is that, during the trial,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0113", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:54,600", "end": "00:05:57,680"}, "text": "there is potentiation happening in the synapses,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0114", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:05:57,680", "end": "00:06:01,480"}, "text": "in the corticocortical synapses, but in anticipation", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0115", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:01,480", "end": "00:06:03,140"}, "text": "for the result, for the reward.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0116", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:03,140", "end": "00:06:07,730"}, "text": "But maybe if the choice that the animal makes is wrong,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0117", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:07,730", "end": "00:06:09,670"}, "text": "then there is actually a reversal", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0118", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:09,670", "end": "00:06:11,650"}, "text": "of that potentiation mediated by this term", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0119", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:11,650", "end": "00:06:15,410"}, "text": "here, which happens through dopamine VTA", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0120", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:15,410", "end": "00:06:18,160"}, "text": "because whether there the animal receives a reward", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0121", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:18,160", "end": "00:06:21,490"}, "text": "or not actually drives the dopamine release in VTA, which,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0122", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:21,490", "end": "00:06:24,075"}, "text": "in turn, drives this reversal or no reversal.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0123", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:27,295", "end": "00:06:30,010"}, "text": "So here, you can see an example of how", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0124", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:30,010", "end": "00:06:34,880"}, "text": "this plasticity rule drives the weight changes over trials.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0125", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:34,880", "end": "00:06:38,840"}, "text": "So here, we have simulated 700 trials of the task.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0126", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:38,840", "end": "00:06:42,940"}, "text": "Each trial is a separate stimulus and one action and one", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0127", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:42,940", "end": "00:06:44,635"}, "text": "reward feedback.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0128", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:44,635", "end": "00:06:46,600"}, "text": "And as you can see, this is an adjacency matrix", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0129", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:46,600", "end": "00:06:49,017"}, "text": "for the weights between the visual cortex and the anterior", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0130", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:49,017", "end": "00:06:49,670"}, "text": "cortex.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0131", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:49,670", "end": "00:06:53,260"}, "text": "And you can see the weight value is changing from the beginning", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0132", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:53,260", "end": "00:06:54,650"}, "text": "to the end of the task.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0133", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:54,650", "end": "00:06:57,330"}, "text": "And likewise, you can see the average weight", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0134", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:06:57,330", "end": "00:07:00,660"}, "text": "in these same synapses actually adapting over time", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0135", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:00,660", "end": "00:07:04,320"}, "text": "and reaching a stable value.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0136", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:04,320", "end": "00:07:08,430"}, "text": "So moving on to the second place, where we have implemented", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0137", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:08,430", "end": "00:07:10,080"}, "text": "synaptic plasticity in this model, that", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0138", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:10,080", "end": "00:07:14,490"}, "text": "is the connections from the anterior cortex to the striatum,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0139", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:14,490", "end": "00:07:19,830"}, "text": "so these connections follow a more sophisticated rule which", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0140", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:19,830", "end": "00:07:22,980"}, "text": "can induce both LTP and LTD.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0141", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:22,980", "end": "00:07:25,170"}, "text": "And essentially, this rule, again,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0142", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:25,170", "end": "00:07:27,850"}, "text": "the changes in weight, the weight gradient.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0143", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:27,850", "end": "00:07:32,430"}, "text": "In other words, it has the typical Hebbian-like component", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0144", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:32,430", "end": "00:07:34,380"}, "text": "where it is a function of the activities", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0145", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:34,380", "end": "00:07:36,310"}, "text": "of the presynaptic and postsynaptic neuron.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0146", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:36,310", "end": "00:07:39,480"}, "text": "But now, this Hebbian component is", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0147", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:39,480", "end": "00:07:43,710"}, "text": "modulated by the DA, the dopamine, released", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0148", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:43,710", "end": "00:07:45,990"}, "text": "in the substantia nigra.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0149", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:45,990", "end": "00:07:48,480"}, "text": "So essentially, here, we have a third region,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0150", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:48,480", "end": "00:07:51,840"}, "text": "this S and C working as a modulator in the connections", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0151", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:51,840", "end": "00:07:55,300"}, "text": "between cortex and striatum.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0152", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:55,300", "end": "00:07:57,430"}, "text": "And there is also a third term, which", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0153", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:07:57,430", "end": "00:08:00,930"}, "text": "actually depends on the current values of these weights.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0154", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:03,700", "end": "00:08:07,990"}, "text": "And as I was saying before, because of this immediate tie", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0155", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:07,990", "end": "00:08:11,080"}, "text": "to dopamine, any reward feedback can actually", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0156", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:11,080", "end": "00:08:15,460"}, "text": "either strengthen the synapses or punishment", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0157", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:15,460", "end": "00:08:18,400"}, "text": "or omission of reward can also weaken the synapses", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0158", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:18,400", "end": "00:08:19,485"}, "text": "and induce LTP.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0159", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:22,300", "end": "00:08:24,850"}, "text": "And also, this rule, you can work out", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0160", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:24,850", "end": "00:08:27,760"}, "text": "the math, which actually you can see in more detail in this paper", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0161", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:27,760", "end": "00:08:29,320"}, "text": "as well.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0162", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:29,320", "end": "00:08:34,299"}, "text": "If you expand on the dopamine term, which", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0163", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:34,299", "end": "00:08:37,510"}, "text": "is essentially dopamine released in S and C,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0164", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:37,510", "end": "00:08:40,460"}, "text": "it has some baseline dopamine plus this epsilon value.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0165", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:40,460", "end": "00:08:42,909"}, "text": "And this epsilon value is, essentially,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0166", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:42,909", "end": "00:08:45,130"}, "text": "the difference between the actual reward", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0167", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:45,130", "end": "00:08:49,170"}, "text": "received and the expected value of the reward to be received.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0168", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:49,170", "end": "00:08:52,970"}, "text": "And this difference shows up in classic reinforcement", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0169", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:52,970", "end": "00:08:55,730"}, "text": "learning tools like Q-learning.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0170", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:55,730", "end": "00:08:57,780"}, "text": "Or even in temporal difference learning as well,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0171", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:08:57,780", "end": "00:09:01,070"}, "text": "you can see a flavor of this plus some extra terms.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0172", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:01,070", "end": "00:09:03,260"}, "text": "So this is a nice result that highlights the fact", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0173", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:03,260", "end": "00:09:06,590"}, "text": "that simpler agent models can actually", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0174", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:06,590", "end": "00:09:11,940"}, "text": "relate to neurobiology through this synaptic plasticity rule.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0175", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:11,940", "end": "00:09:13,670"}, "text": "And here you can see a result, which", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0176", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:13,670", "end": "00:09:17,590"}, "text": "is a hyperparameter search over having two different parameter", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0177", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:17,590", "end": "00:09:18,090"}, "text": "sets.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0178", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:18,090", "end": "00:09:21,720"}, "text": "You can see, in fact, how varying this, essentially,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0179", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:21,720", "end": "00:09:24,350"}, "text": "this prediction error, which is the epsilon, the difference", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0180", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:24,350", "end": "00:09:26,580"}, "text": "between actual value and predicted value.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0181", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:26,580", "end": "00:09:31,430"}, "text": "How does this affect the weight gradient, the delta of the W", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0182", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:31,430", "end": "00:09:32,960"}, "text": "here?", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0183", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:32,960", "end": "00:09:38,390"}, "text": "And how this can reduce both depression and potentiation", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0184", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:38,390", "end": "00:09:41,480"}, "text": "according-- based on the science, essentially,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0185", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:41,480", "end": "00:09:44,375"}, "text": "of the prediction error.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0186", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:44,375", "end": "00:09:47,220"}, "text": "So what we will build here is, again,", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0187", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:47,220", "end": "00:09:51,360"}, "text": "a partial view of the full model in two places.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0188", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:51,360", "end": "00:09:54,970"}, "text": "Initially, we'll work on a model like the second model", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0189", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:54,970", "end": "00:09:57,760"}, "text": "from yesterday, so two cortical regions, a [INAUDIBLE] stimulus", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0190", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:09:57,760", "end": "00:10:01,070"}, "text": "and an ascending system that modulates their activity.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0191", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:01,070", "end": "00:10:03,550"}, "text": "And we will see how Hebbian plasticity", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0192", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:03,550", "end": "00:10:05,060"}, "text": "works with no feedback.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0193", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:05,060", "end": "00:10:07,540"}, "text": "So we will remove the LTP.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0194", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:07,540", "end": "00:10:10,630"}, "text": "There's no LTP reversal because we'll just", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0195", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:10,630", "end": "00:10:13,940"}, "text": "let the system simulate and see how it adapts.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0196", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:13,940", "end": "00:10:19,180"}, "text": "And in the second example, we will include a striatum elements", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0197", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:19,180", "end": "00:10:19,850"}, "text": "as well.", "required": true}
{"unit_id": "sub_0198", "source_type": "subtitle_span", "source_id": "subtitle_srt", "loc": {"start": "00:10:19,850", "end": "00:10:22,450"}, "text": "And in this case, I will do proper reinforcement", "required": true}
